#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1044 expect=skipped domain=XY
#note "The Scope.Classes.Include [FINDINGS] reject pin (no twin fixture exercises the class gate). XY is class=EVENTS, so the rule is out of scope. Declaring '#library custom-domain XY' without XYBLFL present makes the fixture discriminating: were the class gate broken, this custom-Events dataset without --BLFL would fire."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-2
#library custom-domain XY
dataset XY class=EVENTS label="Custom Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col XYSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col XYTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term"
---
S1 | XY | 001 | 1 | SOME EVENT
